{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.TwoSidedIdeal.Kernel"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.one_notMem_traceRadicalIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.one_notMem_traceRadicalIdeal","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L158-L168","doc":"**The radical is proper**: `1` is not in it, so the quotient is nontrivial.  Immediate\nfrom `wtrace 1 = 1`; recorded because a kernel identity alone does not rule out the\ndegenerate case where the projection is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.traceRadicalIdeal_eq_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.traceRadicalIdeal_eq_ker","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L142-L156","doc":"**The trace radical of `wtrace` IS the kernel of the two-row projection**, as\ntwo-sided ideals, for every `n`.\n\nThis is the object-level form of `mem_rad_iff_twoRow_blocks_vanish`.  With\n`twoRowProduct_surjective` it is the full input to the first isomorphism theorem — but see\nthe file docstring: the isomorphism itself is **not** claimed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRow_blocks_vanish_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRow_blocks_vanish_iff","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L122-L140","doc":"**The index bridge.**  `mem_rad_iff_twoRow_blocks_vanish` quantifies over *diagrams*\nwith `n+1` cells; `twoRowProduct` is indexed by *partitions* of `n+1`.  Forward is\ninstantiation at `partitionShape lam`; backward is `exists_partitionShape_eq` followed by\n`subst` — not transport, since `d` is a variable, so no `HEq` is created.  The two\ncardinality proofs that remain differ only as `Prop` terms, which proof irrelevance\ncloses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.mem_ker_twoRowProduct_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.mem_ker_twoRowProduct_iff","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L107-L120","doc":"Kernel membership, unfolded to the blockwise condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L91-L105","doc":"**The two-row projection is onto.**  A component of `twoRowProduct` *is* the same\ncomponent of `heckeProduct`, so this is `heckeProduct_surjective` applied to the tuple that\nextends the target by zero off the two-row blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct_apply","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L85-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.twoRowProduct","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L76-L83","doc":"**The two-row projection.**  `heckeProduct` restricted to the at-most-two-row blocks;\nat convention D these are exactly the blocks the Ocneanu weight does *not* kill. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.TwoRowIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal.TwoRowIdx","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalIdeal.lean#L69-L74","doc":"**The at-most-two-row partitions of `n+1`.**  \"At most two rows\" is spelled\n`rowLen 2 = 0` — row index 2 is empty — matching the hypothesis shape of\n`mem_rad_iff_twoRow_blocks_vanish`.  Note the index shift: `Hecke ℝ q q⁻¹ n` is the algebra\nwhose blocks are partitions of `n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}